PicoGKRuntime 26.2 (0f26321c) — zero-copy mesh hand-off in RenderMesh,
upstreamable to leap71/PicoGKRuntime.

Applied to vendor/PicoGKRuntime by scripts/fetch-deps.sh. Kept as a patch because
it modifies dependency source; no flag-level override exists.

roFloatGridFromMesh copied every vertex and triangle of the input Mesh through
GetVertex/GetTriangle into fresh std::vectors, growing them by push_back with no
reserve, and only then called meshToLevelSet. The copy is serial and runs before
the TBB-parallel mesher starts. The Mesh already stores exactly what the mesher
reads: std::vector<Vector3> is three packed floats per vertex (= Vec3s) and
std::vector<Triangle> three 32-bit indices per triangle (= Vec3I). The patch
passes the two vectors straight to meshToLevelSet, whose QuadAndTriangleDataAdapter
then reads the triangles in place; the one remaining pass over the vertices is
the mesher's own parallel world-to-index transform. The dilated-mesh constructor
in the same file already hands the mesh to openvdb this way; static_asserts pin
the two layouts.

Value-neutral by construction: the same openvdb entry point receives the same
element values in the same order (an int32 index converts to the same uint32,
since indices are never negative), so the level set is unchanged. picovoxel's
G0 grid-hash pins and example pins hold unchanged.

--- a/Source/PicoGKVdbVoxels.h
+++ b/Source/PicoGKVdbVoxels.h
@@ -1029,33 +1029,20 @@
                                                 VoxelSize oVoxelSize,
                                                 int32_t nHalfWidth)
     {
-        std::vector< openvdb::Vec3s >   oVertices;
-        std::vector< openvdb::Vec3I >   oTriangles;
-        
-        for (int32_t n=0; n<oMesh.nVertexCount(); n++)
-        {
-            Vector3 v(0.0f,0.0f,0.0f);
-            oMesh.GetVertex(n, (Vector3*)&v);
-            oVertices.push_back(openvdb::Vec3s( v.X,
-                                                v.Y,
-                                                v.Z));
-        }
-        
-        for (int32_t n=0; n<oMesh.nTriangleCount(); n++)
-        {
-            Triangle t;
-            oMesh.GetTriangle(n, &t);
-            oTriangles.push_back(openvdb::Vec3I(    (unsigned int) t.A,
-                                                    (unsigned int) t.B,
-                                                    (unsigned int) t.C));
-        }
+        // Hand the mesh's own storage to the mesher instead of copying it
+        // element by element into fresh, unreserved vectors. Vector3 and
+        // Vec3s are both three packed floats, and Triangle and Vec3I both
+        // three 32-bit indices, so the mesher reads the same values; the
+        // dilated-mesh constructor above already relies on this layout.
+        static_assert(sizeof(Vector3)  == sizeof(openvdb::Vec3s), "Vector3 must match Vec3s");
+        static_assert(sizeof(Triangle) == sizeof(openvdb::Vec3I), "Triangle must match Vec3I");
 
         openvdb::math::Transform::Ptr roTransform
             = openvdb::math::Transform::createLinearTransform(oVoxelSize);
 
         return openvdb::tools::meshToLevelSet<openvdb::FloatGrid>(  *roTransform,
-                                                                    oVertices,
-                                                                    oTriangles,
+                                                                    (const std::vector<openvdb::Vec3s>&) oMesh.vVertices(),
+                                                                    (const std::vector<openvdb::Vec3I>&) oMesh.vTriangles(),
                                                                     nHalfWidth);
     }
     
